 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-spec-001"></a>
+
+The clinic also publishes its specialties. One page lists every specialty the clinic knows, each under its stored name, together with the veterinarians who hold it `[REQ-SPEC-001]` (stated 2026-08-10). Each holder is named in full: first name, then last name. The whole list is shown on that one page. A specialty no veterinarian holds is still listed, shown as held by none. A veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on the page — the page lists specialties, not the clinic's roster of veterinarians. The page only reads the directory; nothing on it changes a veterinarian or a specialty (NG-2). It is reached by its own address, and no other page links to it. Its wording is subject to `REQ-LANG-002`, as on every other page.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty is listed once, under its stored name, on a single page.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given a specialty held by veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then every holder is shown by first name and last name.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when the directory is opened, then it is listed and shown as held by none.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is not shown.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given the directory, when it is opened, then it offers no way to add, change, or remove a specialty or a veterinarian.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given every other page of the system, when it is rendered, then none of them links to the specialty directory.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. When the clinic knows no specialties at all, the page opens and reports that there are none, rather than failing.
+2. Specialties are presented in a stable order, and so are the veterinarians within each specialty.
+3. A veterinarian holding more than one specialty is shown under each of them.
+4. The page carries the same navigation as every other page, which `REQ-SYS-001` requires.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
